#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128844 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "195aa6d7-fbb5-5b8f-8c0f-0df7a844ad59" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals on Which a Radical Function Is Continuous"}] :question/id #uuid "df4f2e74-d645-5593-8b4a-9dd311c9638e" :question/math-academy-id "e-3597" :question/problem "Determine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\sqrt{4-x}$ is continuous." :question/worked-solution "Our function is a radical function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\sqrt{4-x}$, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n4-x\\geq 0 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow\\qquad x\\leq 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $[MATH: (-\\infty,4]]$, and the function is continuous on this interval."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128845 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eac988ba-ea97-52c7-90a7-d451ee7f49e5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals on Which a Rational Function Is Continuous"}] :question/id #uuid "13d99b42-2152-5484-b0c3-68fcb8917b85" :question/math-academy-id "e-3598" :question/problem "Determine the largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x)=\\dfrac{x-3}{x^2-5x+6}$ is continuous." :question/worked-solution "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= \\frac{x - 3}{x^{2} - 5x + 6} \\\\\n&= (x - 3)/((x - 2)(x - 3)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{x - 2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx \\neq 3\n$$\n\n.\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded points $x=2$ and $x=3$.\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty, 2)$, $(2,3)$, and $(3, \\infty)$, namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty, 2)\\cup(2,3)\\cup(3, \\infty)\n$$\n\nand the function is continuous on these intervals."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128846 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c9958ee-c8b0-5d33-8755-e61cb445b0de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals on Which a Logarithmic Function Is Continuous"}] :question/id #uuid "98c2146d-2e1f-5acc-9774-75aa200cfacb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3599" :question/problem "Find the largest interval of continuity for the function $f(x)=\\log (2x-3) + x^2+1$." :question/worked-solution "The function consists of two parts, a logarithm, and a polynomial.\n\nThe polynomial $x^2+1$ is continuous at all points in its domain, and its domain consists of all real numbers. So, we focus on the logarithm.\n\nLikewise, the logarithmic function $\\log(2x-3)$ is continuous at all points in its domain. However, the logarithm is only defined for positive inputs, so to find its domain, we set the expression inside the logarithm to be greater than zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x - 3 & > 0 \\\\ 2x & > 3 \\\\ x & > \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\log (2x-3) + x^2 + 1\n$$\n\nis continuous on the interval\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac 32,\\infty\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128847 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ad95b4e-e367-5e26-800c-1a87a537ca83" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals on Which a Trigonometric Function Is Continuous"}] :question/id #uuid "0cea3387-1266-5304-9239-bab53a07be8c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3600" :question/problem "The interval $I$ consists of all real numbers $x$ such that $0 \\leq x \\leq 2\\pi$. What is the largest subset of $I$ on which the function $g(x) = \\sin{x}+\\cot{x}$ is continuous?" :question/worked-solution "Trigonometric functions are continuous at all points in their respective domains.\n\nThe function $\\sin{x}$ is continuous over the entire interval $[0,2\\pi]$, but the function $\\cot{x}$ is not defined at\n\n$$\nx=0, \\pi, 2\\pi\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $g(x)$ consists of the union of the intervals $(0, \\pi)$ and $(\\pi, 2\\pi)$, namely\n\n$$\n(0, \\pi)\\cup(\\pi, 2\\pi)\n$$\n\nand the function is continuous on this union of intervals."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ad95b4e-e367-5e26-800c-1a87a537ca83" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals on Which a Trigonometric Function Is Continuous"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b90fa94-1b35-5622-b357-f9af32b8787e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127947} {:answer/id #uuid "95145044-5d83-5eda-9579-137bc6135130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞,-1)∪(-1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127948} {:answer/id #uuid "b7714b6f-54b0-5930-a732-b890a7a26a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞, 1)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127949} {:answer/id #uuid "ea58bfc3-9b73-59f5-aacd-c2e07dcbc1d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 1)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127950} {:answer/id #uuid "35c3d12c-eae1-5a2a-ba8a-a661395de38d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞,-1)∪(-1, 1)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35c3d12c-eae1-5a2a-ba8a-a661395de38d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞,-1)∪(-1, 1)∪(1, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127951} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecca6051-ed35-5aa7-bd5d-c95b40bafebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127946}] :question/id #uuid "bdf79360-c3a2-5f70-b20e-0e9fca989978" :question/math-academy-id "q-39765" :question/problem "Find the largest union of intervals on which the function $f(x) = \\sin (\\frac{3}{x^{2} - 1})$ is continuous."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ad95b4e-e367-5e26-800c-1a87a537ca83" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals on Which a Trigonometri